# Feature Layers

Purpose:
  Define work layers for feature implementation.
  Each layer represents a priority and complexity level.
  AI uses layers to determine what to build next and how.

Owns: ./

Layers:
  L0:
    Name: MVP Core
    Description: Minimum viable product features, already implemented.
    Status: COMPLETED
    Examples: Basic CRUD, authentication, core flows
    WorkMode: Maintenance only

  L1:
    Name: Customer Features
    Description: Features requested by customer after MVP.
    Status: IN_PROGRESS
    Examples: Advanced filtering, reporting, integrations
    WorkMode: Implementation
    Priority: HIGH

  L2:
    Name: Enhancements
    Description: Performance improvements, UX enhancements.
    Status: PENDING
    Examples: Caching, optimization, UI polish
    WorkMode: Implementation
    Priority: MEDIUM

  L3:
    Name: Scalability
    Description: Scaling, multi-tenant, advanced security.
    Status: PENDING
    Examples: Rate limiting, audit logs, multi-region
    WorkMode: Implementation
    Priority: LOW

  L4:
    Name: Innovation
    Description: Experimental features, AI/ML, advanced analytics.
    Status: FUTURE
    Examples: Recommendations, predictions, automation
    WorkMode: Research and POC

Rules:
  [LYR1] Work MUST proceed from L0 -> L1 -> L2 -> L3 -> L4.
  [LYR2] L0 MUST be stable before L1 work begins.
  [LYR3] L1 features MUST be approved by human before implementation.
  [LYR4] Layer assignment MUST be documented in feature decisions.
  [LYR5] Features MAY span multiple layers if justified.

Navigation:
  FeatureDecisions: @decisions.sdd
  ProjectMap: @../projects/{project_name}/MAP.md
  ProjectStructure: @../projects/{project_name}/STRUCTURE.md

State: +
